[Event "Dutch Defense"]
[Opening "Dutch Defense"]
[ECO "A80"]
[Origin "Elias Stein (1789)"]
[Side "black"]
[Tags "d4,sharp"]
[Difficulty "3"]

1. d4 f5 { The Dutch: Black grabs e4 and prepares a kingside attack, at the cost of loosening the king. }
2. g3 { [%name Leningrad] }
( 2. c4 { [%name Stonewall] }
  2... Nf6 3. g3 e6 4. Bg2 d5 { The Stonewall: pawns on c6-d5-e6-f5 give Black a rock-solid grip on e4. }
  5. Nf3 c6 6. O-O Bd6 7. b3 Qe7 8. Bb2 O-O )
( 2. e4 { [%name Staunton Gambit] White gives a pawn for quick development. }
  2... fxe4 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Nc6 5. d5 Ne5 6. Qd4 Nf7 { The knight retreats to defend; Black keeps the extra pawn for now. }
  7. Bxf6 exf6 8. Nxe4 )
2... Nf6 3. Bg2 g6 { The Leningrad: a King's Indian bishop together with the f5 pawn. }
4. Nf3 Bg7 5. O-O O-O 6. c4 d6 7. Nc3 Qe8 { Preparing ...e5 and possibly ...Qh5 for kingside play. }
8. d5 a5 { Securing c5 for the knight (via a6) and stopping b4. } *
